---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_412",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 412,
  "text": "[[1762.1]] <b>336₃.  Randbemerkungen, Unterstreichungen und Exzerpte aus den Epistolae RANDBEMERKUNGEN, UNTERSTREICHUNGEN UND EXZERPTE AUS\n[[1762.2]] DEN EPISTOLAE\n[[1762.19]] <tab/>[ad p. 398] [Ep. II.] Autores non cognoverunt primam causam et originem\n[[1762.20]] omnium rerum, nec veram cognitionem mentis humanae, nec denique veram\n[[1762.21]] causam erroris.\n [[1762.22]] <tab/>[ad p. 399] [Ep. II.] Voluntas non potest esse causa erroris hoc est secundum\n[[1762.23]] Cartesium particularis alicujus volitionis, ideoque volitiones particulares non\n[[1762.24]] possunt esse liberae sed determinantur a causis externis. <Fn><i>Am Rande gestr.</i>: <angle bracket>De Affectibus</angle bracket> <angle bracket> - </angle bracket></Fn> </p>\n<p> [[1762.25]] [p. 463] [Ep. XXVII.] ... Quod autem ad rem attinet, puto me satis clare, et evidenter\n[[1762.26]] demonstrasse, <b>intellectum</b>, <b>quamvis infinitum</b>, <b>ad Naturam naturatam</b>,\n[[1762.27]] <b>non vero ad naturantem</b> <b>pertinere</b>. </p>\n<p> [[1763.1]] [p. 479] [Ep. XXXII.] ... et hoc inde intelligi potest, nempe, quod in rebus nullam\n[[1763.2]] imperfectionem possimus concipere, nisi ad alias res attendamus, quae plus habent\n[[1763.3]] realitatis; et propterea in Adami decreto, quando illud in se consideramus, nec cum aliis\n[[1763.4]] perfectioribus, perfectioremve statum ostendentibus, comparamus, nullam poterimus\n[[1763.5]] invenire imperfectionem; imo <Fn><i>Anstreichung von</i> imo <i>bis</i> zelotypiam</Fn> cum infinitis aliis comparare respectu illius longe perfectioribus,\n[[1763.6]] uti lapidibus, truncis, etc. licet. Et hoc quivis revera quoque concedit: nam\n[[1763.7]] <b>quilibet res, quas in hominibus detestatur, cumque aversione contemplatur,\n[[1763.8]] in animalibus cum admiratione intuetur, uti apum bella, atque\n[[1763.9]] columbarum zelotypiam</i>, etc. quae in hominibus spernuntur, et nihilominus ob ea\n[[1763.10]] animalia perfectiora judicamus. ... </p>\n<p> [[1763.11]] [p. 526] [Ep. XLI.] Nam si (facilitatis gratia) ponamus rationem refractionis esse ut\n[[1763.12]] 3 ad 2, et literas in hac apposita figura, ut eas <b>in parva tua Dioptrica</b> <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: Huddenius</Fn> locas,\n[[1763.13]] appingamus, invenietur, ordinata aequatione, N I, quae dicitur z ^&.SF <Leibniz special character> <wh><zl><i>9 <ne>4</i> <be> zz─xx<whe> ─ <wn>1─xx<wne>.\n[[1763.14]] Unde sequitur, si x ^&.SF <Leibniz special character> 0, erit z ^&.SF <Leibniz special character> 2, quae tunc etiam est longissima. <Fn><i>Leibniz streicht</i> <zl>9 <ne>4 <be> zz</Fn> ... </p>\n<p> [[1763.15]] [p. 528] [Ep. XLII.] ... Imo omnes clarae et distinctae perceptiones, quas formamus,\n[[1763.16]] non <Fn><i>Anstreichung von</i> formamus non <i>bis</i> legibus pendere</Fn> possunt oriri nisi ab aliis claris et distinctis perceptionibus, quae in nobis sunt,\n[[1763.17]] nec ullam aliam causam extra nos agnoscunt. Unde sequitur, quas claras et distinctas\n[[1763.18]] perceptiones formamus, a sola nostra natura, ejusque certis, et fixis legibus pendere, hoc\n[[1763.19]] est, ab absoluta nostra potentia, non vero a fortuna, hoc est, a causis quamvis certis etiam,\n[[1763.20]] et fixis legibus agentibus, nobis tamen ignotis, et a nostra natura, et potentia alienis. ...\n [[1763.21]] <tab/>[ad p. 528] [Ep. XLII.] <i>Omnes clarae et distinctae perceptiones quas formamus,\n[[1763.22]] non possunt oriri nisi ab aliis claris et distinctis perceptionibus quae\n[[1763.23]] in nobis sunt, nec ullam aliam causam extra nos agnoscunt. Unde sequitur\n[[1763.24]] eas ex sola nostra natura ejusque legibus pendere, hoc est ab absoluta ejus\n[[1763.25]] potentia, non vero a fortuna.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1763.26]] [p. 534] [Ep. XLV.] ... Si, exempli loco, aliquis interroget, per quam causam\n[[1763.27]] ejusmodi determinatum corpus moveatur? Respondere licet, id ab alio corpore, hocque\n[[1764.1]] rursus ab alio, et ita in infinitum progrediendo ad talem motum esse determinatum; hoc,\n[[1764.2]] inquam, respondere liberum est, quia duntaxat de motu <Fn><i>Anstreichung von</i> motu <i>bis</i> potest</Fn> Quaestio est, et nos, aliud\n[[1764.3]] corpus continuo ponentes, sufficientem, aeternamque istius motus causam assignamus:\n[[1764.4]] Sed si ego Librum sublimibus meditationibus repletum, nitideque scriptum in manibus\n[[1764.5]] plebei cujusdam conspiciam, et ipsum rogem, unde eum habeat librum, sique mihi, se\n[[1764.6]] eum ex alio libro alterius plebei, qui quoque nitide scribere noverat, descripsisse, et sic in\n[[1764.7]] infinitum procedat, is mihi non facit satis: nam non tantum de figuris, ac ordine litterarum\n[[1764.8]] interrogo, de quibus tantum respondet; verum etiam de meditationibus, et sensu, quem\n[[1764.9]] earundem compositio indicat; nihil ad haec in infinitum sic progrediens respondet. Quomodo\n[[1764.10]] hoc ideis applicari queat, facile ex eo, quod ego in Cartesii <i>Principiorum Philosophiae</i>\n[[1764.11]] Geometrice a me demonstratorum axiomate nono declaravi, percipi potest.\n [[1764.12]] <tab/>(p. 598) [Ep. LXXII.] <i>Materia male a Cartesio definitur per extensionem,\n[[1764.13]] sed debet explicari per attributum quod aeternam seu infinitam essentiam\n[[1764.14]] exprimit.</i> (+ Scilicet non per molem quiescentem. +) </p>\n",
  "number": "336₃.",
  "title": "Randbemerkungen, Unterstreichungen und Exzerpte aus den Epistolae",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:336₃. Randbemerkungen, Unterstreichungen und Exzerpte aus den Epistolae RANDBEMERKUNGEN, UNTERSTREICHUNGEN UND EXZERPTE AUS DEN EPISTOLAE [ad p. 398] [Ep. II.] Autores non cognoverunt primam causam et originem omnium rerum, nec veram cognitionem mentis humanae, nec denique veram causam erroris. [ad ...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>